# --- Claude Code -----------------------------------------------------------
CLAUDE.local.md
.claude/*.local.*

# --- Gradle ----------------------------------------------------------------
.gradle/
build/
# The Kotlin compiler's transient session markers (.kotlin/sessions), written into the project
# directory by the build-logic compilation. Machine-local liveness state, never source.
.kotlin/
!gradle/wrapper/gradle-wrapper.jar

# gradle-wrapper.jar IS committed, deliberately. It is the bootstrapper that
# lets a clean clone build without a preinstalled Gradle. Its integrity is
# protected by the checksums documented in gradle-wrapper.properties, not by
# excluding it from version control.

# NOTE: project-level gradle.properties is deliberately NOT ignored.
#
# It was, and that was wrong: a blanket `gradle.properties` rule silently swallows a
# legitimate committed file (build-wide settings such as org.gradle.caching), and a
# silently-ignored file is worse than an inconvenient one.
#
# Machine-specific configuration — JVM args, proxy or truststore settings, credentials —
# belongs in GRADLE_USER_HOME (~/.gradle/gradle.properties), which is outside the repository
# and therefore cannot be committed by accident anyway.

# --- Java ------------------------------------------------------------------
*.class
*.jar
!gradle/wrapper/gradle-wrapper.jar
*.war
*.ear
hs_err_pid*
replay_pid*

# --- IDE -------------------------------------------------------------------
.idea/
*.iml
*.ipr
*.iws
out/
.vscode/
.settings/
.project
.classpath

# --- Terraform (P15-TSK-013) -----------------------------------------------
# A root's working directory and any local state. infra/scripts/terraform-check.sh writes none of
# these into the tree (TF_DATA_DIR is its own volume), but a hand-run `terraform init` does, and
# state can hold what a resource returns: it lives in the remote backend, never in git.
# .terraform.lock.hcl IS committed, deliberately: it is the provider pin's checksum (ADR-0121).
.terraform/
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
*.tfplan
crash.log
crash.*.log

# --- OS --------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# --- Secrets ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Belt and braces. Secrets must never reach the repository (.claude/rules/security.md);
# P0-TSK-031 adds scanning so this is not the only line of defence.
*.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.jks
*.keystore
secrets/
